# CURATED SEED — committed deliberately. See testdata/rapid/README.md.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: the shortest sequence rapid found that distinguishes
# "ErrAlreadyStopped is clean success" from "ErrAlreadyStopped is a failure" —
# register svc01, arm a genuine failure on it, register svc02 with an
# ErrAlreadyStopped repeat style, then StopAll twice. The failed first pass
# retains the registry; the retry must return nil.
#
# PROVENANCE (measured 2026-08-31): this was recorded while the
# ErrAlreadyStopped filter at service_manager.go:888 was MUTATED AWAY
# (`if stopErr != nil {`). It is a mutation-kill witness, not a defect that was
# ever present on main. Replaying it against that mutation still reproduces the
# original message below after 0 tests.
#
# "[rapid] fail file ... is no longer valid" UNDER -v ON GREEN CODE IS EXPECTED,
# NOT A REGRESSION. t.Repeat records a stream that ends where the failure was,
# so a passing run cannot consume it to the end. The stream is also positional:
# adding or renaming an action changes SampledFrom(actionKeys) cardinality and
# silently re-decodes these bytes into a DIFFERENT sequence.
#
# Because of that erosion, the coverage does not live here. It lives in
# TestStopAllRetryAfterFailedPassTreatsAlreadyStoppedAsClean
# (service/service_manager_prop_test.go), which names the sequence explicitly.
# This file is retained as the provenance record of how it was found.
#
